      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between a Kérastase hair oil and a hair serum?",
            "content": "<p>The oils — <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-elixir-ultime-original-oil\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Elixir Ultime Original Hair Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Elixir Ultime</a>, <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-gloss-absolu-glaze-drops-45ml\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Gloss Absolu Glaze Drops 45ml at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Glaze Drops</a>, <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-chroma-absolu-radiance-hair-oil\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Chroma Absolu Radiance Hair Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Chroma Absolu</a>, <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-chronologiste-parfum-hair-oil\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Chronologiste Parfum Fragrance-In-Hair-Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Chronologiste</a>, and the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-discipline-oleo-relax-serum\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Discipline Oléo-Relax Hair Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Discipline Oléo-Relax</a> — are finishers: applied to dry or towel-dried lengths for shine, frizz control, and softness. The serums are targeted leave-in treatments: the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-8h-magic-night-serum-90ml\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Nutritive 8-Hour Magic Night Serum 90ml at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Nutritive 8-Hour Magic Night Serum</a> nourishes dry hair overnight, and the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-blond-absolu-cicaplasme-150ml\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Blond Absolu Cicaplasme Serum 150ml at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Blond Absolu Cicaplasme</a> fortifies lightened hair and protects it from heat before styling.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is a Kérastase hair oil worth it?",
            "content": "<p>A professional oil is a few-drops product — two or three for medium hair — so a bottle stretches to dozens of uses, and the refillable 75ml formats across the oil range extend it further still. Set against a salon gloss each time you want the finish, a bottle you keep at home is strong value for a salon-grade formula. These are precise tools for a specific result — shine, frizz control, heat protection — rather than everyday basics.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do you apply Kérastase hair oil on wet or dry hair?",
            "content": "<p>The finishing oils — Elixir Ultime, Glaze Drops, Chroma Absolu, Chronologiste, and Oléo-Relax — are made for dry or towel-dried hair, applied to the lengths and ends after styling. The serums keep their own rhythm: Cicaplasme goes onto towel-dried hair before blow-drying or ironing, and the 8-Hour Magic Night Serum onto dry hair at bedtime. None of these go on a soaking-wet scalp; they're for the lengths, not the roots.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which Kérastase oil is best for frizzy hair in the Philippines?",
            "content": "<p>It depends on your hair's weight. For coarse, voluminous, rebellious frizz, the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-discipline-oleo-relax-serum\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Discipline Oléo-Relax Hair Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Discipline Oléo-Relax Hair Oil</a> is purpose-built — a control finishing oil that settles unruly hair through a humid day. For frizz-prone hair that mainly wants mirror shine, finish with the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-gloss-absolu-glaze-drops-45ml\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Gloss Absolu Glaze Drops 45ml at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Gloss Absolu Glaze Drops</a>. And for frizz on fine hair, <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/products/kerastase-elixir-ultime-original-oil\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Elixir Ultime Original Hair Oil at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Elixir Ultime</a> is the lighter choice.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which Kérastase oils come in refillable or travel sizes?",
            "content": "<p>Four of the finishing oils — Elixir Ultime, Chroma Absolu, Chronologiste, and Discipline Oléo-Relax — come as refillable 75ml bottles with matching 75ml refills, so you keep the bottle and replace only the oil (the Glaze Drops comes as its 45ml dropper). Elixir Ultime, Chroma Absolu, and Chronologiste are also available in 30ml travel sizes. Find every format in the <a href=\"https://www.hairmnl.com/collections/kerastase-hair-oil\" title=\"Shop Kérastase Hair Oils at HairMNL\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Kérastase Hair Oils collection</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I use Kérastase hair oil every day?",
            "content": "<p>Yes, with attention to dosage. The Chronologiste Parfum Oil is designed as a daily post-styling finisher; Elixir Ultime, Glaze Drops, and Oléo-Relax can be used daily if you keep to one or two drops on fine hair, two or three on thick. The 8-Hour Magic Night Serum is built for nightly use on dry hair, and Cicaplasme belongs in every heat-styling session. Daily use does no harm — but too much product on fine hair builds up, so let a few drops be enough.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is Kérastase Elixir Ultime a protein treatment?",
            "content": "<p>No — it's a moisturizing, shine oil, not a protein or bond-building treatment. It seals, smooths, and protects from heat, but it doesn't rebuild the internal structure of damaged hair. If your hair needs protein or bond repair after bleaching or harsh processing, pair the oil with a dedicated treatment rather than relying on it alone.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
